  nombreItem: "THE ECHO GAZELLE   Thursday, XXX XXX XXXX  REED CHASE FOUND  Police
    Confirm Death \xB7 Family Asks for Privacy Police confirmed Wednesday evening
    that Reed Chase, 15, who had been missing since Sunday, has died.  Chase was
    reported missing by his parents after he did not return home on the evening of
    Sunday. Authorities and community volunteers had searched the area for more than
    a day. Police said no further details will be released at this time out of respect
    for the family.  \u201CWe are heartbroken,\u201D the Chase family said in a brief
    statement. \u201CReed was kind, creative, and loved by us. We ask for privacy
    as we grieve.\u201D  Chase was a sophomore at XXXXXX High School and a member
    of the school\u2019s art club. In a statement, school officials called him \u201Ca
    quiet, thoughtful student\u201D and said counselors will be available to students
    and staff beginning Friday.  A vigil is being planned for Saturday evening, and
    details will be announced through the school.  \u201CIf you or someone you know
    is struggling, please talk to a parent, teacher, or counselor, or contact a local
    crisis line.\u201D"
  portada: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 5ee8b117e5af0e94ab3d3cccd50d662e, type: 3}
